  <data name="Shell_ReplaceWithVerifiedBackup.Content" xml:space="preserve"><value>Replace originals; retain verified backups</value><comment>Verified backup means retained bytes were reopened and checked against the observed source revision before replacement. It is not a guarantee against physical-media or device loss.</comment></data>
  <data name="Shell_RequirePerfectTransform.Content" xml:space="preserve"><value>Require a perfect coefficient transform</value><comment>Lossless means transforming existing quantized JPEG coefficients without decoding/re-encoding or new quantization. It does not promise identical file bytes, and partial coding units may prevent a perfect transform.</comment></data>
  <data name="Shell_TrimPartialMinimumCodedUnits.Content" xml:space="preserve"><value>Trim partial minimum coded units</value><comment>Minimum coded unit is JPEG's component-sampling coding unit, not necessarily an 8 by 8 pixel block. Trimming permanently discards the exact source-space edge pixels shown in review; consent is required.</comment></data>
  <data name="Shell_PreserveSourceScans.Content" xml:space="preserve"><value>Preserve source scans</value></data>
  <data name="Shell_SequentialDct.Content" xml:space="preserve"><value>Sequential DCT scans</value></data>
  <data name="Shell_ProgressiveDct.Content" xml:space="preserve"><value>Progressive DCT scans</value><comment>Progressive DCT stores frequency coefficients across multiple JPEG scans. This choice reorganizes scans without re-quantization; it does not increase image quality or describe animation.</comment></data>
  <data name="Shell_ReviewInstruction.Text" xml:space="preserve"><value>Changing any processing choice requires a new analysis and fresh trimming consent.</value></data>
  <data name="Shell_RecursiveExclusionNotice.Text" xml:space="preserve"><value>Recursive analysis excludes proven app-owned output and backup folders. Traversal observations appear with the review.</value></data>
  <data name="Shell_BackupDestinationLabel.Text" xml:space="preserve"><value>Verified backups will be retained at:</value></data>
